uld parents be looking for so  certainly you want to look for the signs  of the food right so fever abrupt onset  cough runny or stuffy nose sore throat  headache muscle aches but also in  children they can have things like  stomach pains or nausea and vomiting and  diarrhea abdominal symptoms and then you  want to recognize when things might be  getting worse so if the kid complains of  muscle aches or pains if they look like  their lips or skin are turning blue  they're having respiratory difficulties  their fevers very high or their mental  state or  this really changes you need to seek  care and call your doctor and as you  pointed out this thing look can look  like it's going away and then it can  suddenly roar back the flu shot dr. Tara  Narula thanks  you
 

